---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Button from "../../components/Button.astro";
import SectionMessage from "../../components/sectionmessage.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Matt Rabah is a Detroit-based CX, customer success, and implementation professional focused on customer lifecycle systems, CRM discipline, and practical AI workflows."
>
  <section class="container section hero">
    <div class="stack-300">
      <p class="heading-xxs text-brand">About</p>
      <h1 class="heading-xxl" style="max-width:18ch">
        I build the operating layer customers feel.
      </h1>
      <p class="body-l measure">
        My work sits between CX, customer success, implementation, and CRM
        discipline — with practical AI layered in where it earns its place.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section container--prose">
    <header class="section-head"><h2 class="heading-l">Background</h2></header>
    <div class="stack-300">
      <p class="body-l">
        I've spent seven-plus years across NeuroSync, Shinola, and Context By
        Design. The thread is simple: customers feel the operating model. They
        feel the handoff, the missed note, the unclear owner, the delayed
        follow-up, and the moment a team has to rediscover what should already
        be known.
      </p>
      <p class="body-l">
        I've worked across healthcare accounts, high-touch client experience,
        portfolio growth, Salesforce process, lifecycle diagnostics, onboarding,
        retention systems, and executive-facing account work. Different
        industries, same problem: customer experience breaks when ownership is
        vague.
      </p>
      <p class="body-l">
        I hold an M.S. in Customer Experience Management from Michigan State
        University's Eli Broad College of Business and a B.S. in Organizational
        Behavior from Oakland University. I'm a Salesforce Certified Platform
        Administrator, with additional certifications in business intelligence
        and inbound marketing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section container--prose">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="heading-l">Current focus</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="stack-300">
      <p class="body-l">
        My current focus is practical AI in customer-facing operations. Not AI
        as a novelty layer, but AI as a way to reduce administrative drag,
        prepare better, surface risk earlier, and help teams make cleaner
        decisions without blurring accountability.
      </p>
      <p class="body-l">
        Healthtech, medtech, and other regulated environments are strong fits,
        because trust is fragile there and implementation discipline matters.
        But the broader work is the same everywhere: customer lifecycle design
        for complex teams. Clear owners, usable systems, better handoffs, and
        fewer surprises near renewal.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section container--prose">
    <SectionMessage appearance="information" title="Open to new roles">
      I'm currently open to roles in customer success, CX, implementation, and
      RevOps-adjacent work. If that's what you're hiring for, I'd like to hear
      about it.
      <div slot="actions">
        <Button href="/contact" appearance="primary" spacing="compact"
          >Start a conversation</Button
        >
      </div>
    </SectionMessage>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hero {
      padding-block: clamp(var(--space-800), 12vw, 7rem);
    }
    .measure {
      max-width: 46rem;
      color: var(--color-text-subtle);
    }
    .section-head {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-300);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
